# Bash-sequence equivalent of `make wipe_and_prep_emulator`: wipe the
# emulator, reinstall, and disable idle auto-exit - see CLAUDE.md's
# "Always use `make wipe_and_prep_emulator` instead of bare `pebble wipe`"
# note for why the idle-exit push matters for a scripted walkthrough.
# `pebble install` auto-launches the app, so no button press is needed
# here.
#
# IMPORTANT: every sequence that imports this file needs an
# `APP_TEST_HOOKS=1 pebble build` (native runs only - the containerized/
# golden path already defaults this, see `run-sequence-in-container.sh`'s
# own `APP_TEST_HOOKS="${APP_TEST_HOOKS:-1}"`). This used to only matter
# for the wakeup_conflict_*.seq walkthroughs (which needed
# TestBlockedSystemWakeupMinuteOffsetsPos/Neg specifically), but since the
# TestSetTimerIndex/State/Remaining backdoor and the
# TestSetTimerRemainingDisplay/TestSetClockDisplay/
# TestSetLaunchElapsedDisplaySec display-override family used throughout
# this suite are ALL gated behind APP_TEST_HOOKS too (see main.c's
# `#ifdef APP_TEST_HOOKS` blocks in inbox_received()), a plain `pebble
# build` silently no-ops every one of those AppMessages - if a walkthrough
# that imports this file shows unexpected/live values instead of the
# expected static ones, check this first before suspecting the feature
# itself.
KILL
WIPE
INSTALL
SLEEP 3

# Deliberately does NOT pin the EMULATOR's own clock via `emu-set-time`.
# An earlier version of this file (and a since-retired
# wipe_and_prep_golden.seq variant) tried that: repinning the DISPLAYED
# clock backward to a fixed reference after pebble-tool's own connection-
# triggered resync had already moved it forward to the real host time
# (confirmed: TAP/APPMSG trigger that resync, SCREENSHOT/emu-set-time
# itself do not - see lib/steps.sh) creates a backward-then-forward clock
# discontinuity that Pebble OS's real wakeup subsystem interprets as the
# watch having been off, producing the genuine system "While your Pebble
# was off..." screen instead of this app's own alarm screen - corrupting
# any sequence that also waits for a REAL timer to fire. The
# TestSetClockDisplay/TestSetTimerRemainingDisplay/
# TestSetLaunchElapsedDisplaySec overrides each individual walkthrough
# sends before its own screenshots sidestep that failure mode entirely,
# by design - they're APP-SIDE rendering overrides (see main.c's
# inbox_received()), never touch the real emulator/system clock, so they
# can't trigger that discontinuity and work identically for every
# sequence, including alarm_*.seq/
# wakeup_conflict_natural_fire_while_open.seq - expiry/wakeup logic always
# uses the real clock regardless of this.
#
# IdleExitSec=0 (key 10011) disables idle auto-exit. See
# emulator_configuration.mk for the full settings key numbering; only the
# ones this sequence actually needs are repeated here to avoid coupling
# this framework to that Makefile-specific file.
APPMSG --int 10011=0
